  "description": "The extremes of the declared range, in one account. TRAN-CAT-BAL is PIC S9(09)V99, so the largest value it can hold is 999999999.99: at fifteen percent that is an exact quotient of 12499999.999875 and a stored 12499999.99, which fits TRAN-AMT's own S9(09)V99 exactly and would overflow anything narrower. The second category takes the smallest non-zero balance a scale-2 field can carry, 0.01, at the twenty-five percent discgrp.txt row 1 declares for category 0002, and the whole of its 0.000208... is discarded. Both records belong to account 1, so there is no break between them and no rewrite at all - the accumulated 12499999.99 is carried in WS-TOTAL-INT to a flush that :219-221 never performs. The two identifiers ascend with WS-TRANID-SUFFIX because :474 increments it before every write.",
